The neutrino oscillation experiments reveal that the three lepton flavors consist of the two mass-mixed states and an exponentially growing hot dark matter component. This hot dark matter component is mostly relevant for the neutrino masses, which are generated by the interactions with the electrons and the quarks via the so called seesaw mechanism. The relevant parts of the Lagrangian invariant under the Abelian family gauge group $	ext{U}(2)_{L} 	imes 	ext{U}(2)_{R} 	imes 	ext{U}(1)_{B-L}$ are $$ egin{aligned} -\mathcal{L}_{l, mass} = \overline{l}_{L} \widetilde{m}_{l} l_{R} +  rac{	ext{1 }}{\Lambda} \overline{
u}_{L} M_{R} 
u_{R} + 	ext{h.c.} \;, \; M_{R} = 	ext{diag} (M_{1}, M_{2}, M_{3}) \end{aligned}$$ where the family index R refers to the right-handed neutrino, L to the left-handed lepton doublets, $\widetilde{m}_{l}$ is the mass term for the charged leptons and $M_{R}$ that of the right-handed neutrinos. The neutrino mass matrix can be written in the block form $$ egin{aligned} M_{
u} = \left(  egin{matrix} A & B & B \ B & C & D \ B & D & C \end{matrix} ight) \cong  rac{\Lambda^{3}}{M_{Pl}^{2}} \left(  egin{matrix} 0 & B & B \ B & D & D \ B & D & C \end{matrix} ight) \;. \label{Mnu}\end{aligned}$$ Assuming that the off-diagonal entries of the neutrino mass matrix $B$ and $D$ are very small the neutrino mass eigenstates $
u_{1}$, $
u_{2}$ and $
u_{3}$ are approximately mixtures of the electron neutrino $
u_{e}$ and the two Majorana neutrinos $
u_{R1}$, $
u_{R2}$. For the diagonalization of the neutrino mass matrix one can use the CKM quark mixing matrix to transform the left-handed weak charged fermions into the mass eigenstates. In the similar way, one can transform the neutrino fields to mass eigenstates by the mixing matrix which can be parameterized with the two angles $	heta_{12}$, $	heta_{13}$, and a $CP$ violating phase $\delta_{13}$. This mixing matrix is the Pontecorvo-Maki-Nakagawa-Sakata (PMNS) matrix. The neutrino oscillation experiments like T2K, NOvA and ICARUS give rise to some restrictions on these mixing angles
